%% Resource resolution and cache lifecycle state diagram
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> RuntimeActive: CanvasRuntime active

  state "Active resource runtime" as RuntimeActive
  note right of RuntimeActive
    Resource descriptors are committed document input.
    App-owned images are external input. DocumentStoreKernel
    owns descriptor tables. ResourceKernel owns dirty ids,
    resolved-image cache entries, and resolver calls only.
    There is no file, network, or asset IO.
  end note

  RuntimeActive --> ResolveRequested: main paint image record carries resourceId
  RuntimeActive --> DescriptorMutation: CanvasEdit or loadDocument success mutates descriptors
  RuntimeActive --> DirtySignal: markResourceDirty(id) or markAllResourcesDirty()
  RuntimeActive --> Disposed: dispose()

  state "Resolve request" as ResolveRequested
  ResolveRequested --> DescriptorSnapshot: Frame/Runtime reads descriptor snapshot

  state "Descriptor snapshot" as DescriptorSnapshot
  note right of DescriptorSnapshot
    The committed-state owner reads resource descriptors and
    passes immutable descriptor facts to ResourceKernel.
    The resolver cannot create, remove, or update descriptors.
  end note

  DescriptorSnapshot --> MissingDescriptor: descriptor missing
  DescriptorSnapshot --> AppKeyDescriptor: CanvasImageResource source is appKey

  state "Missing descriptor" as MissingDescriptor
  MissingDescriptor --> PlaceholderResult: return bounded placeholder

  state "appKey descriptor available" as AppKeyDescriptor
  note right of AppKeyDescriptor
    v1 descriptors expose app-owned resource identity:
    resourceId plus appKey and descriptor metadata.
  end note

  AppKeyDescriptor --> CacheLookup: lookup ImageResolveCache

  state "Cache lookup" as CacheLookup
  note right of CacheLookup
    ImageResolveCache admission is keyed strictly by
    resourceId + resourceRevision. Resource dirty
    invalidates affected entries and advances visual revision.
  end note

  CacheLookup --> CachedResolved: cache hit with ui.Image
  CacheLookup --> CachedNull: cache hit with null or missing for resourceId + resourceRevision
  CacheLookup --> CacheMiss: cache miss

  state "Cached resolved result" as CachedResolved
  CachedResolved --> ResolvedVisual: use app-owned image reference

  state "Cached null result" as CachedNull
  CachedNull --> PlaceholderResult: use bounded placeholder

  state "Cache miss" as CacheMiss
  CacheMiss --> SyncResolverCall: call CanvasResourceResolver.resolveImage

  state "Synchronous app resolver call" as SyncResolverCall
  note right of SyncResolverCall
    The resolver is the only external read boundary in paint.
    It is synchronous, app-owned, and must not mutate runtime,
    Store, CanvasDocument, descriptors, selection, or preview.
  end note

  SyncResolverCall --> ReentrantMutationRejected: app attempts public runtime mutation
  SyncResolverCall --> NullResult: app returns null
  SyncResolverCall --> ResolvedResult: app returns ui.Image

  state "Reentrant mutation rejected" as ReentrantMutationRejected
  note right of ReentrantMutationRejected
    Public runtime mutation from inside the resolver throws
    StateError and produces no document, selection, preview,
    cache, repaint, or action effect.
  end note
  ReentrantMutationRejected --> SyncResolverCall: resolver continues or unwinds without accepted mutation

  state "Null resolver result" as NullResult
  NullResult --> CacheNullResult: remember null/missing by resourceId + resourceRevision and no same-frame retry
  CacheNullResult --> PlaceholderResult: return bounded placeholder

  state "Resolved resolver result" as ResolvedResult
  ResolvedResult --> CacheResolvedResult: store app-owned image reference
  CacheResolvedResult --> ResolvedVisual: return resolved visual

  state "Resolved visual" as ResolvedVisual
  note right of ResolvedVisual
    The engine may cache and paint the reference, but the
    application still owns the ui.Image and its disposal.
  end note
  ResolvedVisual --> RuntimeActive: paint completes

  state "Placeholder fallback" as PlaceholderResult
  note right of PlaceholderResult
    Missing descriptors and unresolved/null images paint a
    bounded placeholder. They do not trigger full-document
    repaint loops or repeated resolver retry in the same frame.
  end note
  PlaceholderResult --> RuntimeActive: paint completes

  state "Descriptor mutation path" as DescriptorMutation
  note left of DescriptorMutation
    Descriptor mutation is admitted only through normal
    rollback-safe edit or staged load. It is not a resolver
    side channel and does not use legacy architecture as source.
  end note
  DescriptorMutation --> DescriptorRevisionChanged: atomic install succeeds
  DescriptorRevisionChanged --> DescriptorCacheInvalidated: resourceRevision/projection effects
  DescriptorCacheInvalidated --> RuntimeActive: main repaint if used

  state "Resource dirty signal" as DirtySignal
  note left of DirtySignal
    Dirty marks external visual content stale only.
    It does not mutate CanvasDocument, resource descriptors,
    selection, preview, or action streams.
  end note
  DirtySignal --> VisualRevisionChanged: increment resourceVisualRevision
  VisualRevisionChanged --> DirtyCacheInvalidated: evict target resource or all entries
  DirtyCacheInvalidated --> RuntimeActive: schedule main repaint

  state "Disposed runtime" as Disposed
  note right of Disposed
    Dispose clears runtime resource caches and dirty state.
    Later resource resolution cannot revive cache state,
    revive caches, call the app resolver, or mutate Store.
  end note
  Disposed --> Disposed: dispose again / no side effects
  Disposed --> Disposed: later resolve, dirty signal, edit, load, or pointer sample / StateError

  note left of RuntimeActive
    Negative invariants:
    no engine-owned file, network, asset-bundle, or remote load,
    no sync glue between duplicate resource sources,
    no direct Store mutation from CanvasResourceResolver,
    no accepted public runtime mutation from inside resolver,
    no document action from resource dirty invalidation,
    no descriptor mutation outside edit/load path,
    no legacy source is normative for new resource behavior.
  end note
